PyMatching reusable matching core modifications
================================================

This branch is based on PyMatching v2.3.1, upstream commit e27b8c6a.

Changes:
- add a Stim-free static matching core;
- add reusable whole-graph f64 and exact u32 reweight/decode APIs;
- reset mutable matching state between repeated decodes; and
- provide a dependency-free CMake build and native contract tests.

Runtime improvements, 2026:
- retain arena allocation slots between reusable-core decodes;
- reset only reached search nodes in the reusable-core reset path;
- bind shortest-path adjacency entries directly to topology edges; and
- retain assertions in Release contract tests and cover arena object lifetimes.

The original no-argument Mwpm::reset retains its full-reset semantics.

Opt-in reuse and recurrence support, 2026-09-30:
- add typed independent sparse-update and retained-matching options;
- reuse exact quantization and skip unchanged graph-weight stores;
- preserve unaffected frozen region hierarchies with strict-gap invalidation;
- cold-reset on widespread changes or zero-cost edges becoming positive;
- add explicit sequence reset and exception cleanup;
- expose canonical live-state snapshots without allocator-history dependence;
- add matching_reuse and matching_snapshot sources and native contract tests.
